 > of SYS_sysinfo and defines it, or something.

Yup, SYS_sysinfo needs to be added to the kernel entry table (and
appropriate header files).  I'm suprised this hasn't caused problems
earlier on already.  I'll do this ASAP (both libc and the kernel).

 > > * Structure sigaction has no member sa_restorer.

 > Huh ?  This really confuses me.  Is this necessary for OSF/1
 > compatibility ?  How am I to write code that works right on both
 > systems, if I refuse to use #ifdef ?

Yes, it is necessary for OSF/1 compatibility.  I suspect that Linus is
discouraging the use of the sa_restorer field since it seems to be
Linux specific.  Why does your program need that field?  To switch
stacks on signal delivery?  If you let me know what exactly the
problem is that requires using this field I'd be happy to work with
you on finding an #ifdef free solution.

	--david

